{
  "name": "serialization-contract-object-types",
  "description": "A serializer reads the data members of every object type a serialized value's static type names, and of every object type reached from those members' types: an interface, an object type a type alias declares and a class alike, through a union, together with a class's toJSON method and no other method. A value passed to a rest parameter typed any[] of a function the analyzed program does not declare is read the same way. Beside them, an interface member no serialized value carries is reported, and of two members a string literal names, the one looked up through a receiver typed with a string index signature is reported while the one looked up through an any-typed receiver is retained.",
  "languages": ["ts"],
  "target_kind": "application",
  "expect": [
    {
      "symbol": "Payload.id",
      "report": "none",
      "retained_by": [
        "serialization-contract"
      ]
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Payload.inner",
      "report": "none",
      "retained_by": [
        "serialization-contract"
      ]
    },
    {
